<<<
tint, shade, hue. All are available as substitutes for the dominant word colour.
===
**tint**, *shade*, *hue*. All are available as substitutes for the dominant word *colour*.
>>>

<<<
Different hues are, so far as meaning goes, simply different colours, so called because for good or bad reasons the everyday word is held to be unworthy of the context.
===
Different *hues* are, so far as meaning goes, simply different colours, so called because for good or bad reasons the everyday word is held to be unworthy of the context.
>>>

<<<
Different tints & shades are properly speaking not different colours but varieties of any particular colour, tints produced by its modification with various amounts of white, & shades by various admixtures of black.
===
Different *tints* & *shades* are properly speaking not different colours but varieties of any particular colour, *tints* produced by its modification with various amounts of white, & *shades* by various admixtures of black.
>>>

<<<
have a growing influence in determining the choice of a synonym for colour.
===
have a growing influence in determining the choice of a synonym for *colour*.
>>>

